  <h3>Conclusion</h3><p>World Suicide Prevention Day 2025 reminds India that suicide is not merely a personal tragedy but a public health crisis demanding urgent systemic action. While initiatives like Tele-MANAS and MHCA 2017 mark progress, prevention requires multi-sectoral coordination — between government, communities, and individuals. For aspirants, this issue illustrates the intersection of governance, social justice, and ethics in policy-making.</p>
